  "details": "I would love to see custom scripts being usable in vrc. UDON is a nice way to code but its stillway to limited and most importantly way to slow. I made a test where i coded a udon script that simply rotated a cube on update. With udon i took me 0.057 micro seconds per frame per cube, but with a custom script just 0.0008 micro seconds. This may seem to not that bad and indeed it isnt but remember that this is just a single cube rotation. Imagine a huge and complex script to as example implement a specialgame mechanic. This smal times sum up to a bad performance wich is realy bad. In terms of sequrity im sure there is a way to make a library/dependency whitelist to as example lock the funktion to read/write on hard drive.",
